    (:gap
      :id "GAP-946797"
      :target "asl/packages/asl-ir/src/lowering.asl#lowerAstNode"
      :lens :verification
      :auditor "google/gemma-4-31b-it:free"
      :temp 0.55
      :severity :critical
      :hazard "Reentrant lowering callback allows AST node lowering to recursively invoke itself through dynamic import resolution, causing unbounded stack growth and memory/VFS transaction leakage via premature commit of partial IR state."
      :evidence "In lowerAstNode, the function calls resolveImportPath which may trigger module loading; if a module being loaded references symbols in the same module currently being lowered, lowerAstNode re-enters before the VFS transaction for the outer call completes. No reentrancy guard or transaction isolation boundary exists."
      :remediation "Introduce a lowering context stack with explicit reentrancy detection: maintain a set of in-progress module paths; abort with a diagnostic if a path is encountered twice. Wrap each lowering pass in a VFS transaction that only commits after all recursive lowering completes, ensuring atomic IR construction and preventing partial state leakage."
      :confirmations 1
      :status :open
      :firstSeenAt 1789946797009
      :lastSeenAt 1789946797009)
  
